\": 13811,\n      \"word_count\": 2443,\n      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"children\": [],\n      \"characters_present\": [\n        \"Prince Prospero\",\n        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a gruesome plague marked by bleeding pores and rapid death, prompting Prince Prospero to retreat with a thousand courtiers into a fortified, elaborately designed abbey to escape contagion. Inside, seven uniquely colored rooms—each with stained-glass windows matching their decor—are illuminated by external firelight, creating eerie, shifting hues, except for the final black chamber with blood-red windows and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting all merriment and inducing dread. At a grand masked ball during the fifth month of seclusion, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, triggering terror and outrage among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black chamber, where the figure is found to be empty, revealing the plague has infiltrated the sanctuary. One by one, the revellers die as the clock stops and the lights fade, leaving darkness and decay in dominion.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"the mummer\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a bold and robust man who presides over a lavish gathering in a secluded abbey, displaying authority and a strong reaction to perceived insult. He initially demonstrates leadership by confronting a masked figure, but his demeanor shifts to rage and fear when pursued, ultimately leading to his death. His actions and reactions are shaped by the escalating tension and the mysterious presence of the masked intruder.\",\n          \"source_position\": 10339,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero is bold and robust\",\n          \"quote\": \"the prince was a bold and robust man\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He reacts with anger and demands punishment for the masked intruder\",\n          \"quote\": \"Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He is visibly affected by fear and rage when confronted by the intruder\",\n          \"quote\": \"the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice\",\n          \"position\": 12389,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He attempts to confront the intruder directly, leading to his death\",\n          \"quote\": \"turned suddenly and confronted his pursuer\",\n          \"position\": 12980,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He dies after being stabbed by the intruder\",\n          \"quote\": \"the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\",\n          \"position\": 12980,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 6,\n      \"confidence\": \"hig